WEBVTT

1
00:01.333 --> 00:04.500
Your agent is waiting.
And you're not at your desk.

2
00:04.967 --> 00:07.667
Termote
Your Terminal, Anywhere.

3
00:07.867 --> 00:15.167
Two commands. One QR code.
Install, start on your network, scan it with your phone.

4
00:15.367 --> 00:22.333
A real terminal, built for thumbs.
Any shell, any CLI agent. Keys for Esc, Ctrl and arrows; swipe left for Ctrl+C, right for Tab.

5
00:22.533 --> 00:32.500
Chat with Claude Code and Codex.
Send the next message, see that it works, answer its questions with one tap.

6
00:32.700 --> 00:38.667
OpenCode, too.
Its status, its chat, slash commands and permission answers, the same way from your phone.

7
00:38.867 --> 00:42.667
Pick up any session again.
Every Claude Code and Codex session of the folder: resume it, fork it, see the files it changed.

8
00:42.667 --> 00:46.833
Know what it costs.
Tokens and an estimated cost for each session, today and this week.

9
00:47.033 --> 00:49.833
Who changed each line.
Blame in the file viewer, beside the agent's own edits.

10
00:49.833 --> 00:52.667
One click to the commit.
Its message, author and hash, ready to copy.

11
00:52.867 --> 01:00.500
See exactly what changed.
Browse the files, preview Markdown and diagrams, review the agent's diff.

12
01:00.700 --> 01:06.667
Herdr or tmux. Every agent, one place.
Herdr workspaces with each agent's status, or your tmux sessions: the same Chat, Files and Changes.

13
01:06.867 --> 01:12.833
A worktree for each task.
Branch off into a new worktree and workspace, so agents never step on each other.

14
01:13.033 --> 01:16.833
All your machines, one sidebar.
Reach the Termote of another computer over SSH: its sessions, Files and Changes.

15
01:16.833 --> 01:20.667
Keep an eye on the host.
CPU, memory, disks and battery, a tap away in the header.

16
01:20.867 --> 01:23.167
Send files from your phone.
Upload with a button, a drop or a paste.

17
01:23.167 --> 01:25.833
Deleted by mistake?
It waits in the trash: restore it, or delete it for good.

18
01:26.033 --> 01:30.833
Panes side by side.
Split, zoom, swap and resize them from the Pane menu, on tmux, Herdr and Zellij.

19
01:31.033 --> 01:34.833
A desktop layout your way.
A compact or detailed sidebar you can resize, the toolbar in the header or on the right.

20
01:34.833 --> 01:38.667
Right-click for more.
Copy a path, rename, download, or open a file in Windows.

21
01:38.867 --> 01:45.833
Light or dark, three styles.
Neutral, Terminal or Native. Export your settings, import them in another browser.

22
01:46.033 --> 01:48.167
Run the project's tasks.
npm, make, Go, Gradle, Maven, Cargo and more: one tap, in a tab of its own.

23
01:48.167 --> 01:50.333
Tiếng Việt, too.
The whole app in English or Vietnamese, picked in Settings.

24
01:50.533 --> 01:53.333
Get pinged when it's done.
A push when an agent finishes or needs you.

25
01:53.333 --> 01:56.167
Share a view-only device.
A one-time code pairs a tablet or a teammate's phone, without the password.

26
01:56.367 --> 02:00.667
Private by default.
Listens on 127.0.0.1 by default · Password or paired devices · View-only role · Tailscale HTTPS · Signed releases

27
02:00.933 --> 02:06.167
Your Terminal, Anywhere.
curl -fsSL https://termote.ohnice.app/install.sh | sh
termote.ohnice.app · Open source, MIT
